  "startedAt": "2026-10-24T04:32:16.049Z",
  "steps": [
    "Opening and checking the legacy schema3 animation leaves it unchanged. Selecting instance then returning to scene before review clears the local change; Cancel preserves every author file and source draft.",
    "The explicit instance selection reviews only schemaVersion and playbackScope while all tracks, clips, IDs, values and loops remain equal. The actual Rust schematic preview accepts the v4 named clip. Chinese, English and Japanese at390px preserve the focused selector node, choice, approval and sampled clip time without horizontal overflow. Cancelling the reviewed change writes nothing.",
    "Apply modifies only the ordinary source draft; Save writes exactly the reviewed BOM/CRLF animation. Every scene, assembly, registration, template, image and other author file remains byte-identical.",
    "Reopening the saved v4 source restores its instance choice. Reviewing a return to scene changes only playbackScope and retains schema4; cancelling keeps the saved instance setting intact.",
    "Saved scene preview captures the exact schema4 source. Switching its temporary mode from whole scene to instance and back, selecting a clip and seeking does not change the runtime playbackScope or any author file.",
    "The real saved-byte build capture produces animation subplan3 and animation.instances2d for both scene and assembly. The actual adapter generator explicitly rejects standalone instance-scope scene generation; project assembly remains parent schema1. No Godot process is executed."
  ],
